 "Certification & Competence Framework": "/training/certification",
 "What each Adjudix certificate actually attests to — published plainly, so a client evaluating a certificate-holder knows exactly what they're trusting.": "/training/certification",
 "A working understanding of every ADR mechanism and how outcomes are implemented. Eligible for all.": "/training/certification",
 "Arbitrator": "/training/certification",
 "Competence to conduct a hearing and issue a reasoned, enforceable award under the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure.": "/training/certification",
 "Conciliator": "/training/certification",
 "Competence to actively propose and help finalize settlement terms both parties accept.": "/training/certification",
 "Mediator": "/training/certification",
 "Competence to facilitate a settlement the parties reach themselves, without proposing terms.": "/training/certification",
 "Competence to draft enforceable dispute resolution clauses for commercial contracts.": "/training/certification",
 "Competence to run a hybrid process from mediation through to a binding award, keeping each phase's confidentiality intact.": "/training/certification",
 "How certification connects to the panel and membership": "/training/certification",
 "Completing a track is the entry route into <1>Professional Panel</1> eligibility and <2>Associate membership</2>. Certification alone doesn't guarantee panel appointment — panelists are also vetted for experience and conduct — but it is the defined starting point.": "/training/certification",
